(window.DETAIL_C = window.DETAIL_C || {})["mth-12-12"] = {"mth-12-12-m01":{"idea":"Add up thin strips under the curve.","steps":["Each thin strip has height f(x) and width dx, so its area is f(x) dx.","Add the strips from x = a to x = b.","That sum is the definite integral from a to b."],"others":"The end value times the width treats the curve as flat. The difference of end values is the change in f, not an area. Swapped limits would change the sign.","trap":"Strips, then integrate.","answer":"the integral of f(x) dx from a to b"},"mth-12-12-m02":{"idea":"Area is a size, so it cannot be negative.","steps":["A definite integral can be negative when the curve is below the axis.","The area is its absolute value.","Area is measured in square units."],"others":"Area cannot be negative. A region below the axis still has positive area. Area is not measured in length units.","trap":"Square units, never negative.","answer":"positive, and are measured in square units"},"mth-12-12-m03":{"idea":"Integrate x from 0 to 2.","steps":["The integral of x from 0 to 2 is [x²/2] = 2.","It is also a right triangle with base 2 and height 2.","(1/2) × 2 × 2 = 2."],"others":"1 and 1/2 come from using the wrong base or height. 4 is the area of a square of side 2.","trap":"Triangle area has the factor 1/2.","answer":"2 square units"},"mth-12-12-m04":{"idea":"Integrate x² from 0 to 3.","steps":["The antiderivative is x³/3.","At 3: 27/3 = 9. At 0: 0.","The area is 9 square units."],"others":"9/2 would come from integrating 3x. 3 and 27 forget to divide by the new power or forget to cube.","trap":"x³/3, then put in 3.","answer":"9 square units"},"mth-12-12-m05":{"idea":"One arch of the sine curve lies above the axis.","steps":["The integral of sin x from 0 to π is [−cos x].","−cos π − (−cos 0) = 1 + 1 = 2.","The curve is above the axis on the whole arch, so the area is 2."],"others":"4 would be two arches. 0 would be the integral over a full cycle. 1 is the area for a quarter arch.","trap":"One arch is 2.","answer":"2 square units"},"mth-12-12-m06":{"idea":"The line y = x is below the axis on the left, so split at 0.","steps":["The integral of x from −1 to 1 is 0, but only because the two parts cancel.","Each part has area 1/2.","The total area is 1/2 + 1/2 = 1."],"others":"0 is the integral, not the area. 2 doubles the whole area. 1/2 is just one part.","trap":"Cancelling parts do not cancel in area.","answer":"1 square unit"},"mth-12-12-m07":{"idea":"x³ is odd, so the two parts have equal area.","steps":["The curve is below the axis for negative x.","By symmetry, the area is 2 times the integral of x³ from 0 to 1.","That is 2 × 1/4 = 1/2."],"others":"1 doubles one more time. 1/4 is only one part. 0 is the integral, not the area.","trap":"Double the positive part.","answer":"1/2 square unit"},"mth-12-12-m08":{"idea":"Write √x as x^(1/2) and integrate.","steps":["The antiderivative is (2/3)x^(3/2).","At x = 4: (2/3) × 8 = 16/3.","At 0 it is 0, so the area is 16/3."],"others":"8 forgets the factor 2/3. 4 is the width of the interval. 8/3 uses 4^(3/2) = 4 by mistake.","trap":"4^(3/2) = 8.","answer":"16/3 square units"},"mth-12-12-m09":{"idea":"The parabola is symmetric about the x-axis, so double the upper half.","steps":["The upper half is y = 2√x.","Its area from 0 to 4 is 2 × (2/3) × 8 = 32/3.","Double for both halves: 64/3."],"others":"32/3 is the upper half only. 16/3 uses y = √x. 128/3 doubles twice.","trap":"Count both halves.","answer":"64/3 square units"},"mth-12-12-m10":{"idea":"When x is given in terms of y, use horizontal strips.","steps":["Each strip is horizontal, with length x and thickness dy.","Its area is x dy.","The limits are values of y, from c to d."],"others":"y dy has the wrong strip length. x dx does not match the limits in y. y dx is for vertical strips.","trap":"Horizontal strips: integrate x dy.","answer":"x dy, with y running from c to d"},"mth-12-12-m11":{"idea":"A strip's height is the upper curve minus the lower curve.","steps":["Height of a strip is f(x) − g(x).","Integrate from a to b.","Take the absolute value so the area is positive."],"others":"A difference of products has no geometric meaning. A sum of the curves is the wrong height. A product of the curves is also wrong.","trap":"Upper minus lower.","answer":"the absolute value of the integral of [f(x) − g(x)] dx from a to b"},"mth-12-12-m12":{"idea":"Find where the curves meet, then integrate the difference.","steps":["x = x² gives x = 0 and x = 1.","Between 0 and 1 the line is above the parabola.","Area = the integral of (x − x²) from 0 to 1 = 1/2 − 1/3 = 1/6."],"others":"1/12 and 1/3 and 1/2 come from missing or wrong terms.","trap":"Upper minus lower.","answer":"1/6 square unit"},"mth-12-12-m13":{"idea":"The line y = 4 is above the parabola between x = −2 and 2.","steps":["x² = 4 gives x = ±2.","Area = the integral of (4 − x²) from −2 to 2.","By symmetry, 2 × (8 − 8/3) = 32/3."],"others":"16/3 is half the area. 64/3 doubles it. 16 is a rectangle of width 4 and height 4.","trap":"Use symmetry to halve the work.","answer":"32/3 square units"},"mth-12-12-m14":{"idea":"Use one quadrant and multiply by four.","steps":["The area in one quadrant is the integral of √(a² − x²) from 0 to a.","That equals πa²/4.","Four quadrants give πa²."],"others":"πa²/2 is a semicircle. πa is a length-like value. 2πa² is too large.","trap":"Area is πr².","answer":"πa² square units"},"mth-12-12-m15":{"idea":"An ellipse is a circle stretched in the y direction.","steps":["Start with the circle x² + y² = a², with area πa².","Multiply the y-values by b/a.","The area is multiplied by b/a, giving πab."],"others":"π(a + b) is not an area. πa²b has the wrong dimension. 2πab is twice the area.","trap":"Circle is the special case a = b.","answer":"πab square units"},"mth-12-12-m16":{"idea":"Use horizontal strips with x = √y.","steps":["Solve y = x² for x: x = √y in the first quadrant.","Area = the integral of √y dy from 0 to 4 = (2/3) × 8.","That is 16/3. Vertical strips give 4 × 2 − 8/3 = 16/3 too."],"others":"32/3 would be the area on both sides of the y-axis. 8 and 4 come from rectangles.","trap":"The area is between the curve and the y-axis.","answer":"16/3 square units"},"mth-12-12-m17":{"idea":"Area is always positive.","steps":["Below the axis the integral is negative.","Take its numerical value.","That positive number is the area."],"others":"Keeping the minus sign would give a negative area. Halving is not part of the method. The area is not zero just because the curve is below the axis.","trap":"Absolute value of the integral.","answer":"the numerical value of the integral, which is positive"},"mth-12-12-m18":{"idea":"Add the two half-arches as positive areas.","steps":["From 0 to π the area above the axis is 2.","From π to 2π the area below the axis is also 2.","Total area = 2 + 2 = 4, while the integral is 2 − 2 = 0."],"others":"2 counts only one arch. 0 is the integral. 8 doubles the total.","trap":"Split at the axis crossing.","answer":"4 square units"},"mth-12-12-m19":{"idea":"The graph of |x| and y = 2 form a triangle.","steps":["y = |x| and y = 2 meet at x = ±2.","Area = the integral of (2 − |x|) from −2 to 2 = 8 − 4 = 4.","It is also a triangle: (1/2) × 4 × 2 = 4."],"others":"6 and 8 use the wrong base or height. 2 is half the area.","trap":"Base 4, height 2.","answer":"4 square units"},"mth-12-12-m20":{"idea":"Integrate eˣ from 0 to 1.","steps":["The antiderivative is eˣ.","At 1: e. At 0: 1.","The area is e − 1, about 1.718."],"others":"e + 1 adds instead of subtracting. 1 forgets the extra area. e forgets to subtract the lower value.","trap":"Subtract e⁰ = 1.","answer":"(e − 1) square units"},"mth-12-12-m21":{"idea":"Integrate 1/x from 1 to e.","steps":["The antiderivative is log x.","log e − log 1 = 1 − 0.","The area is 1."],"others":"e − 1 would be the integral of 1. log 2 uses the wrong upper limit. e is the upper limit itself.","trap":"log e = 1.","answer":"1 square unit"},"mth-12-12-m22":{"idea":"Find the intersections, then integrate upper minus lower.","steps":["x² = x + 2 gives x = −1 and x = 2.","The line is above the parabola in between.","Area = [x²/2 + 2x − x³/3] from −1 to 2 = 10/3 − (−7/6) = 9/2."],"others":"9 doubles the area. 4 and 27/2 come from wrong arithmetic.","trap":"Watch the negative lower limit.","answer":"9/2 square units"},"mth-12-12-m23":{"idea":"Parts above and below the axis have opposite signs.","steps":["Find where the curve crosses the x-axis.","Split the integral at those points.","Add the numerical values of the pieces."],"others":"Subtracting the part below gives a wrong total. Doubling does not fix the cancellation. A single integral can cancel parts.","trap":"Absolute value of each piece.","answer":"split the integral at the points where the curve crosses the axis, and add the numerical values"},"mth-12-12-m24":{"idea":"The line y = 2x makes a right triangle.","steps":["The integral of 2x from 0 to 3 is [x²] = 9.","It is also a triangle with base 3 and height 6.","(1/2) × 3 × 6 = 9."],"others":"18 forgets the factor 1/2. 6 and 3 use one of the sides only.","trap":"Height is y at x = 3, which is 6.","answer":"9 square units"},"mth-12-12-m25":{"idea":"The intercepts give the base and the height.","steps":["The line meets the axes at (2, 0) and (0, 2).","Area = the integral of (2 − x) from 0 to 2 = 4 − 2 = 2.","Also (1/2) × 2 × 2 = 2."],"others":"4 forgets the factor 1/2. 1 and 1/2 are too small.","trap":"Right triangle with legs 2 and 2.","answer":"2 square units"},"mth-12-12-n01":{"idea":"Integrate and subtract limits.","steps":["The integral is [x³/3 + x] from 0 to 2.","At 2: 8/3 + 2 = 14/3.","14/3 = 4.667 square units."],"trap":"Do not forget the +x term.","answer":"4.667"},"mth-12-12-n02":{"idea":"The curve stays above the axis, so a plain integral works.","steps":["3x² − 2x + 1 has no real roots, so it is always positive.","The integral is [x³ − x² + x] from 0 to 2.","At 2: 8 − 4 + 2 = 6 square units."],"trap":"Check the sign first.","answer":"6"},"mth-12-12-n03":{"idea":"Find the meeting points, then integrate upper minus lower.","steps":["The curves meet at x = −1 and x = 2.","Area = [x²/2 + 2x − x³/3] from −1 to 2.","= 10/3 + 7/6 = 27/6 = 4.5 square units."],"trap":"Subtract the lower limit value, which is negative.","answer":"4.5"},"mth-12-12-n04":{"idea":"Use the circle area formula πa².","steps":["The radius is a = 5, since a² = 25.","Area = πa² = 25π.","25π = 78.54 square units."],"trap":"a is the root of 25.","answer":"78.54"},"mth-12-12-n05":{"idea":"Use the ellipse area formula πab.","steps":["From x²/9 + y²/4 = 1 we get a = 3 and b = 2.","Area = πab = 6π.","6π = 18.85 square units."],"trap":"a and b are roots of the denominators.","answer":"18.85"},"mth-12-12-n06":{"idea":"Integrate eˣ from 0 to log 3.","steps":["The antiderivative is eˣ.","At log 3: e^(log 3) = 3. At 0: 1.","The area is 3 − 1 = 2 square units."],"trap":"e^(log 3) = 3.","answer":"2"},"mth-12-12-n07":{"idea":"Use symmetry about the origin.","steps":["The curves meet at x = −1, 0 and 1, and there are two equal regions.","For 0 to 1, the area is the integral of (x − x³) = 1/2 − 1/4 = 1/4.","The total is 2 × 1/4 = 0.5 square unit."],"trap":"Count both regions.","answer":"0.5"},"mth-12-12-n08":{"idea":"Find the meeting points of the two parabolas.","steps":["The parabolas meet at (0, 0) and (4, 4).","Area = the integral of (2√x − x²/4) from 0 to 4.","= 32/3 − 16/3 = 16/3 = 5.333 square units."],"trap":"Upper curve is 2√x.","answer":"5.333"},"mth-12-12-n09":{"idea":"Use horizontal strips.","steps":["The curve meets the line x = 4 at y = ±2.","Area = the integral of (4 − y²) dy from −2 to 2.","= 2 × (8 − 8/3) = 32/3 = 10.667 square units."],"trap":"Integrate with respect to y.","answer":"10.667"},"mth-12-12-n10":{"idea":"cos x is above sin x on this interval.","steps":["Area = the integral of (cos x − sin x) from 0 to π/4.","The antiderivative is sin x + cos x.","(√2/2 + √2/2) − (0 + 1) = √2 − 1 = 0.414 square units."],"trap":"Upper minus lower.","answer":"0.414"},"mth-12-12-n11":{"idea":"The intercepts give a right triangle.","steps":["The line meets the axes at (6, 0) and (0, 4).","Area = the integral of (12 − 2x)/3 from 0 to 6 = (72 − 36)/3 = 12.","Also (1/2) × 6 × 4 = 12 square units."],"trap":"Find the intercepts first.","answer":"12"}};
